  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the r.m.s speed of chlorine molecule is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>490</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>27</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, the r.m.s speed of argon molecules at the same temperature will be (Atomic mass of argon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>39</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>, molecular mass of chlorine <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>)</p>"
